  "preferred_configuration": {
    "prize_parts": [
      {
        "ballot_id": "B018",
        "laureates": [
          "Hidetoshi Katori",
          "Jun Ye"
        ],
        "citation": "for the invention and development of optical lattice clocks"
      }
    ]
  },
  "alternatives": [
    "B011",
    "B040"
  ],
  "statement": {
    "case_for": "My configuration is unchanged. Optical lattice clocks remain the most compelling combination of a sharply identifiable physical solution, demanding experimental realization, and demonstrated scientific maturity. Magic-wavelength confinement addresses the trapping-induced shift while retaining the atom number needed for exceptional precision; Katori represents the central architecture and Ye the defining high-performance experimental development. Independent systems have repeatedly realized the essential capability and have made possible concrete measurements in fundamental physics and geodesy. Formal redefinition of the time standard would be an important institutional consequence, but it is not needed to establish that the physical achievement is mature.",
    "case_against": "The remaining serious reservation is exact credit. Optical-frequency metrology has important contributors beyond the proposed pair, and an archival priority review must distinguish the lattice-clock architecture from broader optical-clock development and subsequent performance advances. The citation should therefore stay narrowly confined to the invention and development of optical lattice clocks, rather than imply credit for all optical-clock progress.",
    "responses": [
      {
        "member_id": "danielsson-ulf",
        "point": "Danielsson gives priority to inflation because of its explanatory reach, while acknowledging that observations do not uniquely establish a microscopic realization.",
        "response": "I accept the extraordinary conceptual reach of B019, but the stated non-uniqueness is material when comparing it with a mature experimental achievement. B018 has a specific mechanism whose predicted measurement capability is realized reproducibly in independent laboratories. This is not a preference for technological utility over fundamental physics; it is a judgment that the lattice-clock principle has both precise physical content and unusually direct experimental closure."
      },
      {
        "member_id": "olsson-eva",
        "point": "Olsson regards the quantum cascade laser as a bounded, mature device invention with broad spectroscopic impact, but questions whether Cho's heterostructure contribution belongs in the proposed attribution.",
        "response": "I agree that B015 is an important and durable instrument innovation. Her attribution concern, however, goes to the central link between the enabling heterostructure work and the specific cascade-laser invention. For B018 the proposed pair maps more directly onto the defining lattice-clock architecture and its decisive realization, subject to the narrower archival review noted above."
      },
      {
        "member_id": "eriksson-olle",
        "point": "Eriksson argues that the quantum spin Hall effect combines a new classification of matter with a landmark experiment, while recognizing uncertainty about the proper experimental representative and the scope of the citation.",
        "response": "B027 has a powerful claim as fundamental condensed-matter physics, but its proposed three-person allocation and the boundary between the quantum spin Hall effect and the wider topological-insulator field need further resolution. Lattice clocks offer a more experimentally delimited object: the same identifiable suppression of confinement shifts has been tested across implementations, with a compact two-person configuration."
      }
    ],
    "uncertainties": [
      "Whether archival priority evidence confirms that Katori and Ye alone are the most exact credit for the lattice-clock architecture and its defining development.",
      "How a final citation can distinguish the lattice-clock achievement from broader optical-clock advances without understating the roles of other pioneers."
    ],
    "conflict_note": "No direct connection to the proposed laureates or apparent conflict is disclosed by the supplied profile."
  }
}
